# Oppvera Watch — remotes and upstream merges

This repo is an educational fork of OneGlanse. Remotes:

- **`oppvera`** → `oppvera/oppvera-watch` — our repo. Push here (`git push oppvera`).
- **`origin`** → `aryamantodkar/oneglanse` — upstream. Fetch/merge only; do not push.

## Upstream merge workflow

1. `git fetch origin`
2. `git merge origin/main` (or rebase only if the user asks)
3. Resolve conflicts, then push to `oppvera`

Clean merges need no intervention. Only act when Git reports conflicts or the user asks for help.

## Conflict resolution policy

**Prefer Oppvera (ours)** when the conflict is fork-specific:

- Branding: Oppvera Watch name, logos, `apps/web/src/lib/branding.ts`
- Docs/README aimed at marketers and GEO learners
- Removed upstream telemetry (PostHog) and related wiring
- Oppvera install/setup guides, org URLs (`oppvera/oppvera-watch`)
- Disabled or fork-specific CI/GitHub Actions

**Prefer upstream (theirs)** when the conflict is core product work:

- New features, APIs, routes, or UI behavior we did not customize
- Bug fixes and security patches in shared application code
- Dependency and tooling updates unless they re-enable removed telemetry

**Combine both** when upstream adds new code in an area we rebranded — take their logic, keep our Oppvera naming/docs where they diverge intentionally.

**Ask the user** when:

- Both sides changed the same business logic and the right merge is unclear
- A change might be a bug fix or a branding/doc edit
- Re-enabling telemetry, analytics, or upstream-only product behavior is involved
- You would drop substantial upstream functionality to keep a local edit

If there is no real conflict (different files or non-overlapping edits), merge silently — do not rewrite working Oppvera customizations.

## After merging

- Verify fork-specific removals still hold (no PostHog reintroduced)
- Push to `oppvera`, never `origin`
